POSTTABLE -- #530 (lcaisalane) kill table 1.  Written after the table finished (table1.out ends KILL530_DONE).

DRIVER   kill530.run-004237.sh (frozen copy of kill530.sh), clone /tmp/gxlca530 (cp -a of build/ holding the #530
         working set), own .MUTANT sentinel.  BASELINE_CMP CLEAN; 14 legs built; clone RESTORED (cmp clean, binary
         fresh, sentinel removed -- re-checked by hand after the run: no .MUTANT, dev_lca.c cmp-clean vs GXEMUL-SEC,
         gxemul -nt dev_lca.c); `restored == base (byte-identical)'; no mutant binary identical to base.
INSTRUMENT  lca_isalane_probe.table1.py (37 rows), md5s in logs/INSTRUMENT.md5.  The SHIPPED probe differs from this
         frozen copy in COMMENTS ONLY: the #530 contract section was added to its header after the freeze (20 diff
         lines; `ast.dump' of the two files is IDENTICAL).  So every score below is the shipped instrument's.
LOAD     two probe lanes, concurrent with #529's kill table 7 (four lanes).  LCAISALANE_RETRIED=none on all 14 legs:
         no session needed its patience retry.

RESULTS (logs/probe_<leg>.raw; check_pred.py: `exact=14 differs=0 of 14 measured (14 predicted)')
   base             37/37   EXACT   (clause (a)'s complement: the fix green)
   head             19/37   EXACT   18 red -- (a) the pre-fix defect verbatim: the six host-death cells + the two
                                    discarded-byte reads + the witness's three reds
   m_exit           22/37   EXACT   15 red -- (b) the removed exit reinstated in the fixed code
   m_declbeyond     30/37   EXACT    7 red -- (d) variant C as a growth mutant of the accept
   m_decleq         24/37   EXACT   13 red -- (d) variant A; `ofs1 zero' is red ONLY because the sentinel was re-pinned
                                    (0x8a has bits 5-6 clear) -- the old 0x0bad1dea would have greened it
   m_writeonlyfold  30/37   EXACT    7 red
   m_readonlyfold   31/37   EXACT    6 red (the byte read past the caller's buffer differed from every want, as predicted)
   m_clamp          35/37   EXACT    2 red -- r23 lane + w23 lane, anchored on r21/w21
   m_lane1          35/37   EXACT    2 red -- ofs2 wide + ofs3 wide (witness rows)
   m_nomask         36/37   EXACT    1 red -- r81 lane, the sole carrier
   m_replicate      33/37   EXACT    4 red
   m_retzero        22/37   EXACT   15 red
   m_lenzero        37/37   EXACT   PREDICTED EQUIVALENT (no len-0 producer) -- DISCLOSED in the contract
   m_andmask        37/37   EXACT   PREDICTED EQUIVALENT on len 1/2/4/8 -- DISCLOSED (split heads unreachable here)

FLOOR    (a) fails pre-fix (head 19/37); (b) fails on the exit reinstated at every fixed site (m_exit, all six cells);
         (c) null medium: the pre-fix file IS the stale copy (head) -- stated rather than claimed as a separate
         comment-only medium, per the open 7n-1 rule question in the flagship queue; (d) the DEPENDS-ON mutants of the
         fix's one position rule (declbeyond, decleq, one-arm folds, clamp, lane/mask edits, retzero) all red;
         (e) the contract is in the probe header, with the two equivalents disclosed by name.
SOLE CARRIERS  r81 lane (m_nomask); r23 lane + w23 lane (m_clamp -- two rows, one mutant); ofs2/ofs3 wide (m_lane1).
CHANNEL LINE, CHECKED (not obeyed): every row's channel was named from source at writing time (PRETABLE item 4) and all
         14 legs landed on prediction -- so for this detector the channel WAS knowable at writing time.  One instance.
